    "title": "Task force to tackle animal cruelty in Fulton County - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Courtney Ward ,\n2 hours ago\nGLOVERSVILLE, N.Y. ( NEWS10 ) — The Fulton County Regional SPCA has relaunched a Fulton County Animal Crimes Task Force to investigate and prosecute reports of animal abuse, neglect and cruelty throughout the county.\nThe multi-agency task force held its first meeting on Sept. 22. The following agencies were in attendance:\nGet the latest news, weather, sports and entertainment delivered right to your inbox! Fulton County Sheriff’s Office Fulton County Emergency Management Saratoga County Sheriff’s Office Fulton County Probation Fulton County Department of Social Services Fulton County district attorney Domestic Violence of Fulton County Gloversville Police Department and Animal Control New York ENCON Johnstown Town Supervisor Christina Vanvalkenburg Survivor Support Services The task force will meet quarterly, and members will receive free training and education throughout the year.\nRead the latest from NEWS10:\nNEWS10 is the Capital Region’s local news leader!\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to NEWS10 ABC.\n1",
